WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.280
Feifei: Hello and welcome to The English We Speak.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:09.900
I'm Feifei.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:10.900
Neil: And I'm Neil.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:13.840
Feifei: In this programme, we're talking about 'about'!

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.420
Neil: About 'about'?

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:16.760
Feifei: About 'about'!

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.700
Neil: This is getting silly! We are indeed talking

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.990
about the word 'about' - but not as it's usually used.

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:27.170
Feifei: Indeed. Let's demonstrate. Is Mark about today?

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:28.760
Neil: Yes, I saw him this morning.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.680
Feifei: So, when I asked: 'Is Mark about today?' I

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.243
wasn't asking if Mark was somehow related

00:00:34.243 --> 00:00:36.930
to the concept of 'today' I just meant, 'Is

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:37.930
Mark here?'

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:41.090
Neil: 'About' means 'here', or 'somewhere near here'.

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:44.749
Feifei: Mark's about. Mark's near here. By the way,

00:00:44.749 --> 00:00:45.749
who's Mark?

00:00:45.749 --> 00:00:47.710
Neil: No idea. But I know he's near here!

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:50.550
Feifei: Well, that's reassuring. Time for some more

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:55.200
examples about 'about'.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.120
Examples: Hi, is Sue about? Just need to give her some

00:00:58.129 --> 00:00:59.929
files.

00:00:59.929 --> 00:01:02.390
Will you be about this evening? I want to

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:04.200
ask a big favour.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:07.700
There's no one about. It's a bit scary.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:13.240
Don't talk like that. There are children about.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:16.300
Feifei: There we are. 'About' meaning in or close

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:17.310
to an area.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.960
Neil: You know, there's another word that behaves

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:19.960
like this.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:21.640
Feifei: You're talking about - 'around'!

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:24.680
Neil: Indeed. We could ask: 'Is Mark around?'

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:26.900
Feifei: And we know the answer to that: you saw him

00:01:26.909 --> 00:01:27.909
this morning.

00:01:27.909 --> 00:01:30.810
Neil: Except - I didn't really see him. Because

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:31.860
Mark doesn't exist...

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.540
Mark: Hi. I'm Mark.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:34.840
Neil: Ah, Mark!

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:37.170
Feifei: We were just talking about you!

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:39.970
Neil: We were just talking about 'about'.

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:40.960
Feifei: And 'around'.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:46.460
Neil, Feifei, Mark: Bye.

